              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Counsel, let's assume that Petitioner did not resign much more than, say, one afternoon and then engaged in this conduct. Do you think you would still be able to make the exact same argument?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9b6985259972ea26a2dc2de9fdff03d5ce94ff5df4d99dca5f0838efc648bcf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9b698525997-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So, Mr. Roth, I understand what you're saying, that the -- that the government didn't prove the kind of facts."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9b6985259972ea26a2dc2de9fdff03d5ce94ff5df4d99dca5f0838efc648bcf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9b698525997-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: So you're asking for a bright line even if it leads to the situation Justice Kagan hypothesizes?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9b6985259972ea26a2dc2de9fdff03d5ce94ff5df4d99dca5f0838efc648bcf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9b698525997-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Gorsuch, jUSTICE GORSUCH: Yeah. Where do they come from, is my question."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9b6985259972ea26a2dc2de9fdff03d5ce94ff5df4d99dca5f0838efc648bcf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9b698525997-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 65,
              "start": 65
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Okay. I think Mr. Roth would say that's an agent, all right? I mean, because Mr. Roth has a way to deal with that. He -- he says, you know, you don't have to be, like, on the books if there's been that clear a delegation from the principal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9b6985259972ea26a2dc2de9fdff03d5ce94ff5df4d99dca5f0838efc648bcf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9b698525997-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 66,
              "start": 66
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, jUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So please tell me why it can't be simply an agent, meaning, why can't we just simply -- instead of this functional whatever, government official, or reliance and control, as the Second Circuit called it, why can't the charge be something as simple as are you acting as an agent?"
      }
    ],
